From: Hoki local integration <code@lukasrieger.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gatt: preserve peer ownership and validate attribute allocation

Keep bonded subscriptions separate from acquired socket lifetimes. Scope
asynchronous operations to their ATT peer, retain buffers, and cancel callbacks
when their application disappears. Preserve write request completion semantics.
Allocate external descriptors relative to their characteristic and reject
intersecting service ranges.

Upstream-Status: Pending [local regression testing; not submitted]

